---
title: Apple Pie
source: https://foodwishes.blogspot.com/2008/10/my-favorite-apple-pie-recipe-getting.html
author: FoodWishes
tags: [dessert]
cuisine: American
---

Pre-heat the oven to !500F.

Peel @honeycrisp apples{6} and slice them thinly. 

In a large bowl combine with @sugar{3/4 cup}, @cinnamon{1/2 tsp}, @nutmeg{1/2 tsp}, @allspice{1/2 tsp}, and @flour{2 tbsp}. Toss until the apples are evenly coated.

Line a #pie pan{} with @./puff-pastry{1 sheet}, leaving some overhang. Fill the crust with the apple mixture.

With a second @./puff-pastry{1 sheet}, cut a lattice pattern with 10-12 strips.

Place the strips over the apples, weaving them to create a lattice top. Trim and crimp the edges.

Brush the top with @water{} and sprinkle with @sugar{1 tbsp}.

Reduce the oven temperature to !400F and bake for ~{35 minutes} or until the crust is golden brown and the filling is bubbly.
